---Merge a Yjs update into an editor document (service)
---
---Merges a Yjs update into an editor document via the yjs-engine sidecar (ENT-1231): reads the current state, calls the engine, then writes the merged state and its contentJson projection conditional on the row it read being unchanged. On a conflict (another merge landed first, or the key was recreated under a new row) it re-reads and re-merges — safe because CRDT merge is commutative and idempotent — up to a bounded number of attempts, after which it 503s rather than retrying forever. 503 also covers an unreachable, slow, or misbehaving engine; 422 covers non-retryable input — a malformed account id, or an update the engine cannot apply or that exceeds its body cap. Service-only, requires the sync_editor_documents platform grant. Change-description documents are read-only; writes return 403.
